1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,870
The Operating Map has a row that says

2
00:00:01,870 --> 00:00:04,870
‘prepare the Session Option Brief.’

3
00:00:05,420 --> 00:00:07,640
Morgan asks a fair question: what is

4
00:00:07,700 --> 00:00:09,760
this preparation role actually allowed

5
00:00:09,810 --> 00:00:11,110
to read or change?

6
00:00:11,110 --> 00:00:13,440
‘Be careful’ will not answer it.

7
00:00:14,103 --> 00:00:18,057
One Friday, the facilitator note says
'available for review.'

8
00:00:18,242 --> 00:00:24,635
If the agent quietly treats that as permission
to confirm a teacher, the map looks orderly
while the work crosses a boundary.

9
00:00:24,799 --> 00:00:28,212
We need a permission slip someone can inspect
before the next draft.

10
00:00:28,639 --> 00:00:35,487
Chapter Nine names five fields: scope, ceiling,
reversibility, escalation, and expiry.

11
00:00:35,849 --> 00:00:39,630
For Harbor, scope is three cleared course notes
and a draft brief.

12
00:00:39,955 --> 00:00:42,067
The ceiling is preparation only.

13
00:00:42,387 --> 00:00:50,015
The role cannot change the source notes,
approve a memory, book a room, contact a
facilitator, or message participants.

14
00:00:50,347 --> 00:00:56,768
Reversibility means Morgan can withdraw or
revise a draft; it does not promise that a
public message could be undone.

15
00:00:56,960 --> 00:01:00,265
Escalation names Morgan for missing or
conflicting evidence.

16
00:01:00,668 --> 00:01:05,297
Expiry sends the proposed slip back for review
before the next course planning cycle.

17
00:01:05,532 --> 00:01:12,892
The workbook asks us to place an action on an
authority ladder: prepare, recommend, route,
stage, execute.

18
00:01:13,084 --> 00:01:15,309
Our role sits at prepare.

19
00:01:15,572 --> 00:01:23,679
Its proposed slip also names permitted source
IDs, forbidden inputs, the receipt, source
checks, an owner, and a revocation path.

20
00:01:23,892 --> 00:01:26,677
A source that was cleared last week may expire.

21
00:01:26,986 --> 00:01:34,346
A rule written in a prompt is not enough for
our paper design; the permission needs to be
visible beside the job and decision.

22
00:01:34,752 --> 00:01:37,162
This exercise grants no real permission.

23
00:01:37,482 --> 00:01:39,623
Now test the value of the work itself.

24
00:01:39,971 --> 00:01:45,603
Suppose Harbor also has a second paper role
that drafts a daily weather summary for
possible workshops.

25
00:01:45,817 --> 00:01:46,755
Nobody reads it.

26
00:01:46,926 --> 00:01:49,842
It has a clean receipt, but no decision uses
it.

27
00:01:50,069 --> 00:01:57,323
Chapter Ten calls for a Quarterly Cull: proof
delivered, permission current, and would we
build it again today?

28
00:01:57,749 --> 00:02:03,624
The session brief has a named decision and
reviewer, though its value is still only a
classroom hypothesis.

29
00:02:03,867 --> 00:02:05,872
The weather summary fails the proof test.

30
00:02:06,086 --> 00:02:12,272
In this exercise we recommend retirement for
human review; we do not delete a trigger or
revoke a live tool.

31
00:02:12,486 --> 00:02:14,648
A retirement decision needs a person too.

32
00:02:14,890 --> 00:02:24,959
If a real agent existed, a human owner would
review the evidence, sign the sunset, revoke
access, archive governed memory, remove
triggers, and record the change.

33
00:02:25,343 --> 00:02:27,401
Neglect leaves permissions behind.

34
00:02:27,794 --> 00:02:32,423
Here, there is no running agent, no trigger,
and no memory to remove.

35
00:02:32,743 --> 00:02:35,197
Write the proposed decision and its reason.

36
00:02:35,559 --> 00:02:37,607
Keep the external world untouched.

37
00:02:37,820 --> 00:02:42,365
The same human discipline governs adding a
capability and taking one away.

38
00:02:42,599 --> 00:02:43,226
Pause.

39
00:02:43,596 --> 00:02:48,780
Which line in the slip would prevent a
well-written brief from turning into an
unauthorized announcement?

40
00:02:49,015 --> 00:02:51,618
Write the Permission Slip for the preparation
role.

41
00:02:51,875 --> 00:03:02,087
Include each of the five fields, its authority
rung, read and write scope, retention rule,
source check, receipt, approval owner, review
date, and revocation path.

42
00:03:02,400 --> 00:03:07,307
Then run the Quarterly Cull on the session
brief role and the course weather-summary role.

43
00:03:07,648 --> 00:03:12,085
Use the three tests and record keep, narrow, or
retirement proposal.

44
00:03:12,384 --> 00:03:14,484
Use a fictional or approved example.

45
00:03:14,836 --> 00:03:18,611
Do not use private operational data or grant a
real permission.

46
00:04:03,974 --> 00:04:05,723
Save revision six as a draft.

47
00:04:06,022 --> 00:04:09,557
A role's permission and its reason to exist
both need renewal.

48
00:04:10,193 --> 00:04:12,143
Next we will give the work a tighter

49
00:04:12,213 --> 00:04:14,263
requirement packet and decide how a

50
00:04:14,323 --> 00:04:15,493
small team would share it.
